{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1", "content": "i recently watched the movie \"the social network\" and here is my detailed review in all lower case as requested:\n\n**movie title:** the social network\n**director:** david fincher\n**release year:** 2010\n**genre:** biography, drama\n\n**storyline:**\nthe movie tells the story of how facebook came into existence. it focuses on mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a harvard university student who creates a website called \"facemash\" which becomes a huge success. this leads to him being approached by cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer) to create a social networking site for harvard students. however, mark teams up with eduard saverin (played by andrew garfield) to create \"thefacebook\", which eventually leads to a legal battle over the ownership of facebook.\n\n**acting:**\n- jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg gives a brilliant performance, portraying mark's intelligence, arrogance, and vulnerability perfectly.\n- andrew garfield as eduard saverin brings depth to the movie with his emotional portrayal of the character's downfall.\n- armie hammer plays the twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss seamlessly, making it hard to believe it's one actor playing both roles.\n\n**direction and cinematography:**\ndavid fincher's direction is impeccable, making the movie engaging from start to finish. the cinematography is top-notch, capturing the atmosphere of harvard and the intensity of the legal battles.\n\n**script:**\naaron sorkin's script is witty and fast-paced, making the technical aspects of creating a website interesting and accessible to all viewers.\n\n**music:**\ntrent reznor and atticus ross's soundtrack complements the movie perfectly, enhancing the emotional and tense moments.\n\n**verdict:**\nthe social network is a must-watch for its engaging storyline, superb acting, and excellent direction. it's no